t will use the enum.name() to persit the String. When querying the same field with the same enum, the value used in query is enum.toString(). This causes problems if we have an enum with values:\r\n```\r\n    public enum Status {\r\n        ALIVE(\"He's Alive!\"),\r\n        DEATH(\"Poor guy\");\r\n        \r\n        private final String value;\r\n\r\n        private Status(String value) {\r\n            this.value = value;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        public String getValue() {\r\n            return value;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        @Override\r\n        public String toString() {\r\n            return this.value;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe persisted field will be \"ALIVE\" but the query will try to use \"He's Alive!\"\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nBoth methods should behave the same way, either using the enum name() or enum toString()\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nReproducer: [https://github.com/seseso/mongodb-panache-quickstart](url)\r\n\r\nThere is a test RepositoryPersonTest that shows the behaviour\r\n\r\n**Environment (please complete the following information):**\r\n - Output of `uname -a` or `ver`: Linux\r\n - Output of `java -version`: Java 11\r\n - GraalVM version (if different from Java): Java 11\r\n - Quarkus version or git rev: 1.9.2.Final\r\n - Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`): 3.6.3\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"geoand","id":4374975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNzQ5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4374975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand","html_url":"https://github.com/geoand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geoand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api